@startuml
!include ../../../tools/diagrams/cka-theme.puml
skinparam sequence {
  LifeLineBorderColor #94A3B8
  ParticipantBackgroundColor #EFF6FF
  ParticipantBorderColor #326CE5
  ParticipantFontStyle bold
}
title "Distributed and reliable": a write in a 3-member etcd cluster (Raft)

participant "client\n(kube-apiserver)" as c
participant "etcd-1\nLEADER" as l
participant "etcd-2\nfollower" as f1
participant "etcd-3\nfollower" as f2

c -> l : put /registry/pods/default/web
note over l : only the leader accepts writes;\na follower would forward it here
l -> f1 : append entry to log
l -> f2 : append entry to log
f1 --> l : stored
note over l : 2 of 3 members have it = quorum\n→ entry is committed
l --> c : OK (revision 1042)
f2 --> l : stored (late is fine)

caption <i>A write succeeds once a majority stores it, so any one member can fail without losing data.</i>\n<i>If the leader fails, the followers elect a new one. Lose the majority, and etcd refuses writes rather than risk diverging copies.</i>
@enduml
